    "solution": "Place the blue portal on the exposed western shot wall. A hostile bolt enters it and emerges friendly from the distant orange mouth, reaching the sealed receiver. Advance to the carrier and get aboard; the receiver retracts the lid which had stopped its upward rail. Ride to the high staging ledge. Move over the marked well, relocate the blue portal to its floor, and fall into it. The same orange outlet now turns your long drop into the range needed to clear the moat and land on the wide eastern bank. The reopened lid was necessary for both the ride and that fall.",
    "nearestExisting": "F28 Reply in Passing and B29 The Shield You Send route converted bolts through portals, while B36 Short Runway, Tall Exit prepares a useful entrance velocity. Here the bolt is not a separate lock at the end: its delivery removes the actual horizontal lid which traps the carrier and caps the later falling runway. The same outlet first carries the opening shot, then the knight whose launch the shot made possible.",
    "novelty": "The first passenger through the portal changes the physical journey available to its second passenger. A closed lid is simultaneously a carrier stop and a height limit; opening it creates both the approach and its stored fall momentum.",
